---
description: Do not add host UI state (e.g. focused pulse) onto library chrome types
globs: **/*.ts,**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: true
---

# Host UI state is not a library field

**Incident:** `focused: boolean | null` was added to `ColumnsEditChrome.renderSection`
so a demo pulse animation would run. That field did **not** exist on the library
chrome. Autofocus already lives on `RecursiveEditManager.autofocus` /
`ctx.autoFocused(id)` — the host reads it in **their** `renderEdit` / `renderCard`.

Copying a presentation prop onto a library type:

- Invents a second contract (`focused`) beside the real one (`edit.autofocus`)
- Forces every host of that chrome to speak demo CSS-pulse language
- Looks like a “render prop” fix while smuggling UI state into the package

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — library chrome grows a demo pulse field
renderSection: (args: { …; focused: boolean | null }) => ReactNode
createColumnsEdit: focused: edit.autofocus

// ✅ GOOD — library unchanged; host reads the manager it already got
renderEdit: (props) =>
  hostShell({ pulse: props.edit.autofocus, … })
```

**Test:** if the field exists only so a demo can set `animation` / highlight,
it is not a library argument. Do not alias `edit.autofocus` as `focused` on
chrome bags.

Related: `no-html-outside-demo.mdc`, `no-optional-defaults.mdc`.
